# /alpha (fixture runbook, not a real command)

Two lines were added above the facts since the G2 list was made, so its line numbers are 2 short.

## Phase A: Read (R0)

A read with no gate rests on `alpha read` (search excerpt).

## Phase B: Erase (R3)

<!-- SAFETY GATE [alpha-erase-portal] -->
- **Target:** [DEVICE_NAME]
- **Reversibility:** R3: not reversible once it runs
The erase waits for `alpha erase status` (search excerpt) and fact X-01 says when.

## Phase C: Run a script (R1 to R3)

<!-- SAFETY GATE [alpha-script-portal] -->
- **Target:** [SCRIPT_NAME]
- **Reversibility:** R1 to R3 by script content
The script result shows in `alpha script result` (vendor repo).

## Phase D: Note (R1)

<!-- SAFETY GATE [alpha-note-portal] -->
- **Reversibility:** R1: delete the note
The note is listed under `alpha notes list` (search excerpt).

